window.docContents[136].resolve({"/Sorts/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Sorts":{"contents":"Cvc.lean associates some Lean types to cvc5-sorts Srt through the ToTyp class.\n\nAssociates a Typ to a Type.Typ associated to a type through ToTyp.\n\nToTyp α specifies a Typ-value for α that corresponds to a Srt.But is not a\nSrt as constructing one requires to be in Env: a Srt value is tied to a specific manager.\nThis lets us go from compatible Lean types to Srt directly.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let b ← Srt.of Bool\n  println! \"b := {b}\"\n  let i ← Srt.of Int\n  println! \"i := {i}\"\n  let r ← Srt.of Rat\n  println! \"r := {r}\"\n  let bv ← Srt.of (BitVec 8)\n  println! \"bv := {bv}\"\n\n\nb := Bool\ni := Int\nr := Real\nbv := (_ BitVec 8)\n\n\nSome cvc5-sorts do not map nicely to builtin Lean types however, so cvc.lean has a few custom types\nwith ToTyp instance.In the following, Float refers to Cvc.Float, not the Lean\nbuiltin type for floating point numbers.\n\n#eval Env.runIO do\n  let f ← Srt.of (Float 8 24)\n  println! \"f := {f}\"\n  let arr ← Srt.of (TotalMap Int Rat)\n  println! \"arr := {arr}\"\n  let ff ← Srt.of (FiniteField 7)\n  println! \"ff := {ff}\"\n  let bag ← Srt.of (Bag (Float 8 24))\n  println! \"bag := {bag}\"\n\n\nf := (_ FloatingPoint 8 24)\narr := (Array Int Real)\nff := (_ FiniteField 7)\nbag := (Bag (_ FloatingPoint 8 24))\n\n\nCvc.lean exposes two API-s for terms: Typed and Untyped.\n\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API","header":"2. Sorts","id":"/Sorts/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Sorts"}});